# The operator's timetable, in Island Hop.
# Test trips leave in 300 days with an adult fare of $77, so no traveller books them by chance;
# "Start with: no test trips" removes any that a failed run left behind (e2e/states/no-test-trips.ts).
# Royal Alpha must be in service: it is the only ferry the form offers.

Test: Operator schedules a trip and deletes it again

  Start with: no test trips

  As operator:
    go to schedules page
    click "Add Schedule"
    "Add Ferry Schedule" dialog should be open
    choose "Blowing Point, Anguilla ➔ Marigot, Saint Martin • 25 mins trip" for "Ferry Route"
    choose "Royal Alpha • 112 Seats (CATAMARAN)" for "Assign Ferry"
    type "{in 300 days}T10:00" in "Departure Time"
    type "77" in "Adult Ticket Price"
    click "Schedule Departure"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/operator/schedules
    backend should reply 201 Created
    should see "Departure schedule slot created successfully"
    "Add Ferry Schedule" dialog should be closed
    type "{in 300 days}" in "Filter by date"
    in "Royal Alpha" row, click "Delete Schedule"
    in "Delete Departure Schedule" dialog, click "Delete Schedule"
    backend should receive DELETE /api/v1/operator/schedules/:id
    backend should reply 200 OK
    should see "Schedule slot deleted successfully"


# The state schedules Royal Alpha at 10:00 first; a second trip at 10:10 overlaps it.
Test: A ferry can't be scheduled for two trips at the same time

  Start with: one test trip

  As operator:
    go to schedules page
    click "Add Schedule"
    choose "Blowing Point, Anguilla ➔ Marigot, Saint Martin • 25 mins trip" for "Ferry Route"
    choose "Royal Alpha • 112 Seats (CATAMARAN)" for "Assign Ferry"
    type "{in 300 days}T10:10" in "Departure Time"
    type "77" in "Adult Ticket Price"
    click "Schedule Departure"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/operator/schedules
    backend should reply 400 Bad Request
    should see "This vessel is already scheduled for another voyage during this time window"
    "Add Ferry Schedule" dialog should be open
    press Escape
    type "{in 300 days}" in "Filter by date"
    in "Royal Alpha" row, click "Delete Schedule"
    in "Delete Departure Schedule" dialog, click "Delete Schedule"
    backend should receive DELETE /api/v1/operator/schedules/:id
    backend should reply 200 OK
    should see "Schedule slot deleted successfully"


Test: The trip form stops a trip that arrives before it leaves

  As operator:
    go to schedules page
    click "Add Schedule"
    choose "Blowing Point, Anguilla ➔ Marigot, Saint Martin • 25 mins trip" for "Ferry Route"
    choose "Royal Alpha • 112 Seats (CATAMARAN)" for "Assign Ferry"
    type "{in 300 days}T10:00" in "Departure Time"
    type "{in 300 days}T09:30" in "Arrival Time"
    type "77" in "Adult Ticket Price"
    click "Schedule Departure"
    should see "Arrival time must be later than departure time."
    backend should not receive any request
    "Add Ferry Schedule" dialog should be open
